{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# RAG Evaluation: Precision, Recall, MRR, nDCG, Faithfulness, Answer Relevance Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `precision_at_k(retrieved, gold, k)` - the literal definition."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `recall_at_k(retrieved, gold, k)` - the literal definition."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `mean_reciprocal_rank(retrieved_list_of_lists, gold_list)` - the mean over queries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `ndcg_at_k(retrieved, graded_relevance, k)` - DCG / IDCG with binary or graded gains."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `extract_claims(answer)` - splits an answer into sentence-shaped claims."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `faithfulness(claims, context_texts, judge)` - fraction of claims judged supported."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `answer_relevance(question, answer, judge)` - judge on whether the answer addresses the question."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MockJudge` - deterministic token-overlap judge so the eval runs offline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `evaluate_pipeline(pipeline_fn, qrels, ks)` - the orchestrator that runs every metric."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that runs three pipeline variants (chunker baseline, hybrid retrieval, hybrid + rerank) against the qrels and prints a metrics table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The output shows precision@k, recall@k, MRR, nDCG@k, faithfulness, and answer relevance for each variant in a single metrics table. The hybrid retrieval row beats the chunker baseline on recall; the rerank row beats hybrid on MRR."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a fifth retrieval metric: hit-rate@k. Compare it against recall@k. Explain when they differ.\n2. Implement a graded faithfulness: 0 (unsupported), 1 (partially supported), 2 (fully supported). Update the metric accordingly.\n3. Replace the mock judge with a real model call. Measure the disagreement between the mock and the real judge on the fixture.\n4. Add a query-class slice (\"literal\", \"paraphrased\", \"multi-topic\"). Report per-slice metrics.\n5. Add an \"answer length\" metric and correlate it with faithfulness. Plot the curve."
      ]
    }
  ],
